  "limitations": [
    "No compilation, compiling tests, native application, original/rebuilt interaction, rendering or parity comparison.",
    "Raw Ghidra x86-64 imports omit external callee/data semantics and original Rust types; narrow append/retention windows can end at a deliberately truncated boundary. Analyzed body sets and actual retained PE intervals are recorded separately.",
    "Native replay substitutes primary-height miss, temporary vector allocation, stop-packet construction, deallocation and memcpy; it does not execute OS, filesystem, allocators, native external callees or game code outside the reviewed windows.",
    "The internal u64 chronology is an adapter implementation for stable native-vector order, not a recovered additional native Game field. Live actors retain their paired chronology across low-24-bit GUID and u32 serial wrap.",
    "Plain-u32 leaf fixtures retain a native wrapping counter, without full allocation chronology; live gameplay uses SharedCounter. No claim of arbitrary concurrent native game allocation or a live survivor spanning a complete u64 chronology cycle.",
    "Complete startup/channel/auth/roster/summary/progression and raw ComponentId/global/indirect ownership remain outside this bounded ordering repair."
  ]
